{"cit": [{"id": "cit", "headword": "चित्", "headword_slp1": "cit", "fold": "cit", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "चित् (I) vt. 1P, 10Ā (pres. चेतति, चेतयते) 1. To perceive, to notice, नेषूनचेतन्नस्यंतम् Bt.xvii.16, xv.38; 2. to understand, to know; 3. to recover consciousness.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "चित् (II) vt. 10U (pp. चिंतित; pres. चिंतयति-ते) 1. To think, to consider, to ponder over, to think out, चिंतय तावत्केनापदेशेन सकृदप्याश्रमे वसामः Sak.ii.; 2. to think of, to bring before the mind, तस्मासस्य वधं राजा मनसाऽपि न चिंतयेत् M.viii.381, iv.258; 3. to remember, e.g. सुतेषु दारेषु धनेषु चिंतयन्; 4. to hit upon, to discover, प्रतीकारश्चिंत्यताम् Hit.i.; 5. to discuss, to treat of; 6. to weigh, to discriminate.With अनु-, to think over or about, to ponder over, Bg.viii.8.With परि-, 1. to think, to consider, त्वमेव तावत्परिचिंतय स्वयं कदाचिदेते यदि योगमर्हतः K.S.v.67; 2. to remember, to think of; 3. to hit upon, to discover.With वि-, 1. to think, to consider; 2. to ponder over, to remember; 3. to intend, to determine; 4. to regard, to have regard to, अस्मान् साधु विचिंत्य संयमधनानुच्चैःकुलं चात्मनः Sak.iv.; 5. to hit upon, to discover.With सम्-, 1. to consider, to think, to think over; 2. to diseriminate, to weigh.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "चित् (I) f. 1. Perception, knowledge; 2. the mind; 3. life, i.e. the principle of vitality, चिन्मात्रमूर्तये Bhartr.ii.1; 4. Brahman (n.).", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "citprakfti": [{"id": "citprakfti", "headword": "चित्प्रकृति", "headword_slp1": "citprakfti", "fold": "citprakfti", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "चित्-प्रकृति f. reflection.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "citsvarupa": [{"id": "citsvarUpa", "headword": "चित्स्वरूप", "headword_slp1": "citsvarUpa", "fold": "citsvarupa", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "चित्-स्वरूप (I) n. the supreme soul.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "चित्